---
const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Is my financial data safe?',
    a: 'Your information is protected in layers. Asset details, titles and attached documents are encrypted before they are stored, access is checked on every request so only you and the people you choose can open them, and on your phone you can add a PIN or biometric lock. Your data is hosted on Google Firebase in Mumbai, and you decide who sees each asset.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can strangers see my information?',
    a: 'No. Your information is visible only to you and to the family members, nominees or co-owners you choose. Other eKosha users cannot see it, and you can change or remove access at any time.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Who do you share my data with?',
    a: 'We do not sell your data and we do not show ads. A small number of trusted services each do one job: Google Firebase hosts your data in Mumbai, Resend sends emails, RevenueCat and Razorpay handle subscription payments, PostHog gives us optional usage statistics, and Google Gemini reads a document only if you choose to import one. The full list is in our Privacy Policy.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What happens to documents I upload?',
    a: 'Documents you attach to an asset are encrypted before they are stored, and can be viewed by you and the family you have shared that asset with. Documents you import to pre-fill an entry are read once. Mutual fund and demat statements and their passwords are not stored, and AI reading happens only if you choose it and give permission.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I delete everything?',
    a: 'Yes. You can delete your account at any time from Settings, and our delete-account page explains exactly what is removed.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Who can see my assets?',
    a: 'Only you — and anyone you choose to share with. You control access at the asset level. Each person you invite sees only what you allow them to see, with read-only or edit permissions.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What if I forget my password?',
    a: 'You can recover your account via your registered mobile number using OTP verification. Your encryption keys are derived from your credentials, so a secure recovery flow re-establishes access without exposing your data.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does eKosha work offline?',
    a: 'You can view previously loaded assets offline. Adding or editing assets and syncing with family members requires an internet connection. Your data syncs automatically when connectivity is restored.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Will eKosha remind me about insurance premiums and FD maturities?',
    a: 'Yes. Add the premium due date, policy expiry or maturity date to an asset and eKosha reminds you 7, 3 and 1 day before, and on the due day. Health and life insurance, fixed deposits, PPF, provident and pension accounts and small savings schemes are covered. Anything overdue stays on your Upcoming renewals page until you update the date. Reminders are included on the Free plan.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Will I get a notification for every single asset?',
    a: 'No. If several renewals fall on the same day you get one short summary notification, not one per asset, and it never shows account details on your lock screen. You can turn push or email on or off for reminders, nudges and updates in Settings, and you can mute reminders for a single entry. Muting affects only you — a co-owner still gets theirs.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is there a mobile app?',
    a: 'Yes. eKosha is available as a native Android app and a full-featured web app accessible from any browser. Both are kept in sync in real time.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can my family access eKosha if I am unable to?',
    a: 'Yes — that is exactly what eKosha is built for. Family members you have shared assets with can access their permitted view at any time. For emergency access workflows, the Premium plan includes inheritance allocation and nominee-specific sharing.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How is eKosha different from a password manager?',
    a: 'A password manager stores login credentials. eKosha stores structured financial records — account numbers, policy details, property information, nominees and valuations — organised so your family can find and understand what exists when it matters most.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can eKosha fill in an asset from a document?',
    a: 'Yes. Pick a policy, statement or other document and eKosha suggests the details for the form, marking every suggested field. Nothing is saved until you review and confirm it, and the app asks your permission before the first use. The Free plan includes 3 of these in total; Premium includes 20 a month.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How does mutual fund and demat statement import work?',
    a: 'Upload your CAMS, KFintech, NSDL or CDSL statement and enter its password. You choose which schemes or holdings to import and eKosha creates one asset for each. Only names and identifiers are imported, not values or transactions, and the statement and its password are not stored. The Free plan includes 2 imports in total; Premium includes 12 a month.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I attach documents to an asset?',
    a: 'Yes. Attach policy PDFs, deed photos or statements (up to 5 per asset) to the asset they belong to. Family members you have shared that asset with can view them. The Free plan includes 25 MB of space and Premium includes 1 GB.',
  },
];

// FAQPage structured data so these Q&As are eligible for FAQ rich results.
const faqStructuredData = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map(({ q, a }) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: q,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: a },
  })),
};
---
<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqStructuredData)} />
<section id="faq" class="bg-white py-24">
  <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="text-center mb-5">
      <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-brand-navy mb-4 tracking-tight">
        Frequently Asked Questions
      </h2>
      <p class="text-brand-muted text-lg">Everything you need to know about eKosha.</p>
    </div>
    <!-- Gold rule -->
    <div class="flex justify-center mb-14">
      <div class="w-14 h-1 bg-brand-gold rounded-full"></div>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-3">
      {faqs.map(faq => (
        <details class="group bg-brand-bg rounded-xl border border-brand-navy/10 overflow-hidden" data-faq={faq.q}>
          <summary class="flex items-center justify-between gap-4 px-6 py-5 cursor-pointer list-none font-semibold text-brand-navy hover:text-brand-gold transition-colors">
            {faq.q}
            <svg
              class="w-5 h-5 shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-180 text-brand-muted"
              viewBox="0 0 20 20"
              fill="currentColor"
            >
              <path
                fill-rule="evenodd"
                d="M5.293 7.293a1 1 0 011.414 0L10 10.586l3.293-3.293a1 1 0 111.414 1.414l-4 4a1 1 0 01-1.414 0l-4-4a1 1 0 010-1.414z"
                clip-rule="evenodd"
              />
            </svg>
          </summary>
          <div class="px-6 pb-5 text-brand-muted leading-relaxed text-sm border-t border-brand-navy/8">
            {faq.a}
          </div>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
